SCC: release the external/status interrupt on its reset command

WR0's "reset external/status interrupts" command didn't release a pending
external/status interrupt, so one would stay asserted.  Needed for the
serial break that 0006 sends for the kernel's magic SysRq.

Upstream candidate.

--- src/scc.c
+++ src/scc.c
@@ -490,6 +490,9 @@
         case WR0_RESETTXPEND:
             scc_release_interrupt(ch?RR3_B_TXIP:RR3_A_TXIP);
             break;
+        case WR0_RESET_STAT:
+            scc_release_interrupt(ch?RR3_B_STATIP:RR3_A_STATIP);
+            break;
             
         default:
             break;
